  "fullContentHtml": "\n<div class=\"ast-post-format- single-layout-1 ast-no-date-box\" style=\"height: auto !important;\">\n\n<p><!-- .entry-header --></p>\n<div class=\"entry-content clear\" style=\"height: auto !important;\">\n<div class=\"post-desc\">\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>Short Information :&nbsp;</strong><a style=\"color: #ff0000;\" href=\"https://neet.nta.nic.in/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\">National Testing Agency (NTA)</a></span> has released the NEET UG 2026 Re-Exam City Details on its official website for candidates appearing in the undergraduate medical entrance exam. According to the notification, the <strong>NEET UG 2026 Re-Exam is scheduled to be held on 21 June 2026.</strong> The last date for submitting the online application form was 11 March 2026. <strong>Candidates can access their re-exam details by logging into the portal using their Enrollment Number, Registration Number, or Date of Birth.</strong>&nbsp; Additionally, candidates appearing for the <strong>re-exam may receive an extra 15 minutes to complete the examination.</strong>&nbsp;Candidates who had applied this form can download their NTA NEET UG Re-Exam City Details 2026 from the link given below.</span></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-2\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n\n</div>\n\n</div>\n<div class=\"newtable1\">\n<table style=\"font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; width: 100%;\" width=\"100%\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\">National Testing Agency (NTA)</span></h2>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #008000;\">NTA NEET UG Online Fee Refund 2026</span></h2>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Important Dates</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Application Start Date : <strong>08 February 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Last Date : <strong>11 March 2026 (Extended)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Fee Payment Last Date : <strong>11 March 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Correction Date :&nbsp;<strong>12-14 March 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000; background-color: #ffffff;\">Exam Date : <strong>03 May 2026 (Cancelled)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Fee Refund Date : <strong>22-27 May 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; background-color: #ffff99; font-size: 12pt;\">Re-Exam Date : <strong>21 June 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Exam City Details : <strong>07 June 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Admit Card Available : <strong>Before Exam</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"background-color: #ffffff; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Result :<strong> Will Be Updated Here Soon</strong></span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Application Fee</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">General : <strong>Rs. 1700/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">EWS, OBC : <strong>Rs. </strong><strong>1600/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">SC, ST, PH : <strong>Rs. </strong><b>1000</b>/-</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Out Side India : <strong>Rs. </strong><strong>9500/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Candidates have to pay their Examination Fee Through Debit Card / Credit Card / Net Banking / UPI and Other Fee Payment Mode Only.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-3\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n\n</div>\n<p></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-3\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n\n</div>\n\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>NTA NEET UG Admissions 2026 : Age Limit</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Born on or before 31 December 2009</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Minimum Age<strong> : 17 Years</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Maximum Age<strong> : No Limit&nbsp;</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Age Relaxation as per NTA NEET UG Online Form Rules.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Use <span style=\"color: #000000; background-color: #ffff00;\"> </span>Tool – </span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>NTA NEET UG Admissions 2026 : Course Details</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"color: #008000;\"><strong>Course Name&nbsp;</strong></span>: National Eligibility Cum Entrance Test NEET UG 2026</span></li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #008000;\">Exam Name</span>&nbsp;</strong>: National Eligibility Cum Entrance Test, 2026 (NTA)</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>NTA NEET UG Admissions 2026 : Educational Qualification</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Candidates who have Passed 10+2 Intermediate Exam with Physics, Chemistry, Biology PCB Group of Subjects in&nbsp;any recognized board will be eligible for this Examination.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">All candidates must read the official information completely before applying.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>NTA NEET UG Online Form 2026 : Selection Process</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Selection will be based on Online CBT Examination.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>How To Fill NTA NEET UG Re-Exam City Details 2026</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Check the Important Links section.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Then click on the Re-Exam City Details&nbsp;link.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">After clicking on the link, candidates will be redirected to the Dashboard page.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">In this page candidates have to fill up the following fields with proper details:</span><br>\n<span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Candidate’s Registration Number</strong></span><br>\n<span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Date of Birth</strong></span><br>\n<span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Gender</strong></span><br>\n<span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Verification Code</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Then the candidates will be required to submit the details in order to fill the Re-Exam City Details.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">The candidate can also download their Re-Exam City Details from the official Website.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-3\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n\n</div>\n<p></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"newtable2\">\n<table style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"has-text-align-center\" style=\"text-align: center; padding: 10px 0px;\" colspan=\"4\" data-align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #cc0052;\"><strong>Follow Our Instagram Channel</strong></span></td>\n<td class=\"post-social-link\" style=\"text-align: center; padding: 10px 0px;\" colspan=\"3\" data-align=\"center\"><strong></strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"has-text-align-center\" style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"4\" data-align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #cc0052;\"><b>Join Our WhatsApp Channel</b></span></td>\n<td class=\"post-social-link\" style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"3\" data-align=\"center\"><strong><a href=\"https://whatsapp.com/channel/0029VaAbQf01NCrYADMLt00L\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\">Follow Now</a></strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; padding: 0px;\" colspan=\"7\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3><strong>Important Links</strong></h3>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"tcell\" style=\"text-align: center; padding: 10px 0px;\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"56%\">\n<h4><span style=\"color: #800000;\"><strong>Download Re Exam City Details<br>\n</strong></span></h4>\n</td>\n<td class=\"tcell\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"43%\">\n<h4 align=\"center\"><strong><a href=\"https://examinationservices.nic.in/AdmitCard/AuthForCity/Login?enc=DJ8reokIYhe/x0Hlb6GKa5XSzGUPsZIi2LhCU/OXDNg=\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\">Link 1</a> | <a href=\"https://cnr.nic.in/AdmitCard/AuthForCity/Login?enc=DJ8reokIYhe/x0Hlb6GKa5XSzGUPsZIi2LhCU/OXDNg=\" target=\"_blan